---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";

const title = "About - Opening Guessr";
const description =
    "Opening Guessr is a free anime opening quiz. Listen to opening themes, guess the anime, and play openings from your own MyAnimeList.";
---

<Layout title={title} description={description}>
    <div class="min-h-screen bg-base-200">
        <div class="navbar bg-base-100 shadow-sm px-4 sm:px-6 py-3 min-h-16">
            <div class="navbar-start">
                <a href="/" class="btn btn-ghost btn-sm">
                    <i class="ph ph-arrow-circle-left text-3xl"></i>
                    <span class="hidden sm:inline">Back to game</span>
                </a>
            </div>
            <div class="navbar-center">
                <span
                    class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold text-shadow-primary text-shadow-xs"
                    >Opening Guessr</span
                >
            </div>
            <div class="navbar-end"></div>
        </div>

        <main class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 sm:px-8 py-10">
            <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold mb-4">
                About <span class="text-shadow-xs text-shadow-primary"
                    >Opening Guessr</span
                >
            </h1>
            <div class="space-y-6 text-base opacity-90">
                <p>
                    Opening Guessr is a free anime opening quiz. You hear an
                    anime's opening theme and have to name the anime it's from.
                    It's a project that started for fun to be played on call on
                    discord by me and a few friends. We loved playing <a
                        href="https://aniguessr.com"
                        target="_blank"
                        class="link">Aniguessr</a
                    >'s guess the opening game but the hard difficulty animes
                    were just always too hard and we'd have to keep moving to
                    the next day to keep playing for extended sessions. We also
                    wanted an intergration with our MAL lists so we can guess
                    opening from animes we know we've seen. So Opening Guessr
                    was born.
                </p>

                <div>
                    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-3">How to play</h2>
                    <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1.5">
                        <li>
                            Pick a pool of anime to draw openings from: by
                            <span class="font-medium"> Difficulty</span> (Easy / Medium
                            / Hard, based on Aniguessr's difficulties so can be used
                            for practice lol), by
                            <span class="font-medium"> Popularity</span> (Top 50 to
                            Top 2500), or load your own
                            <span class="font-medium"> My MAL List</span>.
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            Optionally narrow the pool down with a genre filter.
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            Play 5 rounds. Each round plays a 40-second clip of
                            an opening (from about 25s to 65s in). Type the
                            anime's name — autocomplete suggests matches as you
                            type. Press <kbd class="kbd kbd-sm"> Enter</kbd> to submit
                            (<kbd class="kbd kbd-sm">Esc</kbd> closes the suggestions).
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            Get it right to score points, then move on to the
                            next round. Your best 5-round total is saved as your
                            high score in your browser.
                        </li>
                    </ul>
                </div>

                <div>
                    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-3">
                        Audio vs. Video Clue
                    </h2>
                    <p>
                        You start in Audio mode. If you're stuck, unlock the
                        Video Clue to reveal a blurred video of the opening —
                        but because it's a hint, a correct video-clue answer is
                        worth
                        <span class="font-medium"> 500 points</span> instead of the
                        <span class="font-medium"> 1000 points</span> an audio answer
                        earns. You can also open the full opening at any time to watch
                        it unblurred.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div>
                    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-3">
                        Where the data comes from
                    </h2>
                    <p>
                        The anime list, popularity ranks, scores, years, and
                        genres are pulled from the Tenrai API (the top ~2500
                        most popular anime). The opening videos, audio, and song
                        titles/artists come from the{" "}
                        <a
                            href="https://animethemes.moe"
                            target="_blank"
                            rel="noopener"
                            class="link"
                        >
                            AnimeThemes API</a
                        >. The "My MAL List" mode fetches your own list through
                        the MyAnimeList API. All opening media is used for
                        identification and quiz purposes.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div>
                    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-3">Get in touch</h2>
                    <p>
                        Found a broken clip, a wrong title, or just want to say
                        hi? Reach out at{" "}
                        <a href="mailto:bassmmm@proton.me" class="link">
                            bassmmm@proton.me</a
                        > or find me on{" "}
                        <a
                            href="https://x.com/bassmmdotdev"
                            target="_blank"
                            rel="noopener"
                            class="link"
                        >
                            X</a
                        > and the{" "}
                        <a
                            href="https://discord.gg/ut7qEW9aXq"
                            target="_blank"
                            rel="noopener"
                            class="link"
                        >
                            Discord</a
                        >.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </main>
    </div>
</Layout>
